    {CODE:EMBEDDED}
END_FUNCTION

FUNCTION sysMbSTcp_SocketServerInfo: USINT
	{ DE:" The function returns a USINT which indicate the number of current Client connected.
It also returns the max number of Client connetable in MaxClientAllowed parameter.
To refresh these variables the function can to be called again.
" }

	VAR_INPUT
		MaxClientAllowed: @USINT;  { DE:"Max number of Client allowed" }		
	END_VAR

    {CODE:EMBEDDED}
END_FUNCTION

FUNCTION sysLcd_RotateAt180: BOOL
	{ DE:" Calling this function with mode setted at TRUE produce a rotation of 180°
of the visualization on the display. 
Calling this function with mode setted at FALSE restore display visualization at default.
Keys works accordingly to any mode.
This function can be called continuosly in any task.

The function returns a BOOT equal to mode value
" }

	VAR_INPUT
		mode:		USINT;  { DE:"TRUE=upside down, FALSE=nominal" }		
	END_VAR

    {CODE:EMBEDDED}
END_FUNCTION


FUNCTION sysLocalADCs_Fast: INT
	{ DE:" Return local ADC values as 8bit register.
Allowed values for index are 0, 1, ...till max AI present minus one.
For instance to read the AD converter register of AI1 the index has to be 0.

Note that if the controller is an 8DIN firt 6 ADC values will be refreshed
continuosly. The other will be refreshed continuosly in a 200ms windows every 600ms.
In the non refreshing window of 400ms these values will be frozen at last catched sample.
If the controller is an 4DIN all the ADC values will be refreshed continuosly. 

The function returns a UINT which could have the following meanings:
0 to 255  = 8bit value of ADC[index]
-32767    = index out of range , analog input not present
" }

	VAR_INPUT
		index:		USINT;  { DE:"index [0...(max AI present-1)]" }		
	END_VAR

    {CODE:EMBEDDED}
END_FUNCTION

FUNCTION sysUART_Reinit : BOOL
	{ DE:" Reinit serial port run-time.
NOTE: 
-sysUART_Init() function must be called one time in the program before using sysUART_Reinit() 
-sysUART_Reinit() can be called if sysUART_Init() function has returned TRUE and not when a
 sysUART_putbuf() is in progress.

Serial port allowed: 
 0=RS485 On-Board 2
 1=RS485 or RS232 Plug-In
 2=RS485 On-Board 1

Baud allowed:
 2400   [b/s]
 4800   [b/s]
 9600   [b/s]
 19200  [b/s]
 38400  [b/s]
 57600  [b/s]
 76800  [b/s]
 115200 [b/s]
 		
Configuration	value allowed:
(0x02)	= 7 data bits no parity one stop bit		 
(0x03)	= 8 data bits no parity one stop bit		 
(0x06)	= 7 data bits no parity two stop bits		 
(0x07)	= 8 data bits no parity two stop bits		 
(0x0A)	= 7 data bits odd Parity one stop bit		 
(0x0B)	= 8 data bits odd Parity one stop bit		 
(0x0E)	= 7 data bits odd Parity two stop bits	 
(0x0F)	= 8 data bits odd Parity two stop bits	 
(0x1A)	= 7 data bits even Parity one stop bit	 
(0x1B)	= 8 data bits even Parity one stop bit	 
(0x1E)	= 7 data bits even Parity two stop bits	 
(0x1F)	= 8 data bits even Parity two stop bits	 
	
The function return a BOOL which could have the following meanings:
TRUE	=	Done.
FALSE	=	Not done! This can be due to:
		-parameter num is out of range
		-parameter baud is out of range
		-parameter cnf is out of range

" }

	VAR_INPUT
		num  : USINT; { DE:"Serial port number: 0=RS485 On-Board 2, 1=RS485 or RS232 Plug-In, 2=RS485 On-Board 1" }
		baud : UDINT; { DE:"Baud: 2400,4800,9600,19200,38400,57600,76800,115200 [b/s]" }		
		cnf  : USINT; { DE:"Configuration: see function description" }		
	END_VAR

    {CODE:EMBEDDED}
END_FUNCTION




]]>
