					</functionBlock>
					<functionBlock name="StepControllerAnalog" version="1.1.1" creationDate="0" lastModifiedDate="1728912810">
						<title>Step Controller Analog</title>
						<descr>&lt;HTML&gt;&lt;p&gt;The StepController function block can command up to 6 digital outputs either as a linear 
step controller or as a binary step controller. Typically this function block is used 
in electrical heating applications.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The linear / binary mode can be selected by the input xMode. 
xMode is loaded on the rising edge of xEn.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The function block allows to define the minimum ON and minimum OFF time, to prevent 
the output against cycling. The minimum ON and OFF times are for each step identical.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;All steps are immediately switched off, when the alarm input becomes active.&lt;/p&gt;</descr>
						<vars>
							<inputVars>
								<var name="xEn" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Enable input for the algorithm</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="xAlarm" type="BOOL">
									<descr>External alarm</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="uiXc" type="UINT">
									<descr>Output from a PID, analog output (0 to 10000 *0.01%, internally limited)</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="usiSteps" type="USINT">
									<descr>Number of heaters to be connected (1 to 6, internally limited)</descr>
									<initValue>1</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="xMode" type="BOOL">
									<descr>FALSE = Steps in succession   TRUE  = Steps in binary step</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="uiDelayTimeOn" type="UINT">
									<descr>Delay time on for the respective heater (0 to 600 *s, internally limited)</descr>
