					</functionBlock>
					<functionBlock name="ECBlueBasicCOMerrWTD" version="1.0.0" creationDate="0" lastModifiedDate="0" excludeFromBuild="FALSE">
						<descr>This FB can be used to set the Communication error / control signal Watchdog parameter (h17, reg18).

Communication watchdog defines a behavior in case of a communication failure / control signal failure. If the device receives no message or if the control signal is disturbed in a time window, the device will execute the selected function.

Watchdog Mode:
 0: No function (default) = OFF
 1: Fault (K1 function, h15) in case of communication fault (WDT)
 2: Constant speed 1 * in case of communication fault (WDT)
 3: Fault + constant speed 1 * in case of communication fault (WDT)
 4: Fault by E1 Fault ** (only ECblue)
 5: Constant speed 1 by E1 Fault (only ECblue)
 6: Fault constant speed 1 in case of E1 fault (only ECblue)
 7: Switch over to E1 * in case of a communication fault (WDT)
 8: Failure + switch over to E1 * in case of a communication fault (WDT)

After the call of the FB, a PIN/motor reset can be executed by using the related FB. This allows news settings to be taken over.

The configuration message is sent when a transition of xEn from FALSE to TRUE takes place.

The output provides the info on whether the operation has been successful or not.

The ECBlueBasicCOMerrWTD AFB must be put inside the Background task of the PLC.</descr>
						<vars>
							<inputVars>
								<var name="i_xEn" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Transition FALSE -&gt; TRUE changes the settings in the fan.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiZiehlAddress" type="USINT">
									<descr>Ziehl Fan Address. Broadcast not supported. Default: 1.</descr>
									<initValue>1</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiWTDMode" type="USINT">
									<descr>Watchdog Mode. See description for details. Default 0 (no function).</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_uiWTDTime" type="UINT">
									<descr>Watchdog Time in seconds (default 0 = off)</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
							</inputVars>
							<outputVars>
								<var name="q_xChanged" type="BOOL">
									<descr>TRUE if the parameter has been successfully changed.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="q_xWorking" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Change Operation in progress.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="q_xFailed" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Change has failed.</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="q_xWrongInputs" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Inputs out of range</descr>
								</var>
							</outputVars>
							<localVars>
								<var name="i" type="USINT">
									<initValue>250</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="xEn_old" type="BOOL"/>
								<var name="wWTD" type="WORD">
									<descr>WORD to be sent</descr>
									<initValue>65535</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="MsgNum" type="USINT">
									<initValue>10</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="wWTD_Check" type="WORD">
									<initValue>65535</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="uiRet_WTD" type="UINT">
									<initValue>65535</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="uiRet_WTD_Check" type="UINT">
									<initValue>65535</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="j" type="USINT">
									<initValue>250</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="k" type="USINT">
									<initValue>250</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="uiRet_PIN" type="UINT">
									<initValue>65535</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="iPINL2" type="INT">
									<initValue>0010</initValue>
								</var>
							</localVars>
							<localConsts>
								<const name="usiRetries" type="USINT">
