						</sourceCode>
					</functionBlock>
					<functionBlock name="ECBlueBasicSetIO" version="1.0.0" creationDate="0" lastModifiedDate="0" excludeFromBuild="FALSE">
						<descr>This AFB can be used to set the following parameters (IO Setup):
 - Inverting (h10, reg11)
 - E11 Min  (h11, reg12)
 - E12 Max (h12, reg13)
 - E1 Function (h13, reg14)
 - D1 Function (h14, reg15)
 - K1 Function (h15, reg16)

After the call of the FB, a PIN/motor reset can be executed by using the related FB. This allows news settings to be taken over.

The configuration message is sent when a transition of xEn from FALSE to TRUE takes place.

The output provides the info on whether the operation has been successful or not.

The ECBlueBasicSetIO AFB must be put inside the Background task of the PLC.</descr>
						<vars>
							<inputVars>
								<var name="i_xEn" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Transition FALSE -&gt; TRUE changes the settings in the fan.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiZiehlAddress" type="USINT">
									<descr>Ziehl Fan Address. Broadcast not suppoted. Default: 1.</descr>
									<initValue>1</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_xEnE1Inverting" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Invert E1 (10 V - 0 V). Default 0.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_xEnD1Inverting" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Invert D1. Default 0.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_xEnK1Inverting" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Invert K1 (NO: normally open contact). Default 0.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiE11Min" type="USINT">
									<descr>Start value for AI E1 in % over 0-10. Useful range is rescaled accordingly. Default 5%.</descr>
									<initValue>5</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiE12Max" type="USINT">
									<descr>End value for AI E1 in % over 0-10V. Useful range is rescaled accordingly. Default 100%.</descr>
									<initValue>100</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiE1FK" type="USINT">
									<descr>E1 Function. 0: 0-10V / PWM (defaul). Follwing let E1 act as DI. 1: Enable. 3: Limit. 5: SetIntern2. 6: SetIntern3. 13: change rotation direction. 15: fire alarm.</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiD1FK" type="USINT">
									<descr>D1 Function. 0: OFF. 1: Enable (default). 3: Limit. 5: SetIntern2. 6: SetIntern3. 13: change rotation direction. 15: fire alarm.</descr>
									<initValue>1</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_usiK1FK" type="USINT">
									<descr>K1 Function. 0: OFF. 1: Operation. 2: Fault (default). 4: Speed limit ON. 17: Control Bit 15 (h1). 20: fault indication or indication for active temperature management</descr>
									<initValue>2</initValue>
								</var>
							</inputVars>
							<outputVars>
								<var name="q_xChanged" type="BOOL">
									<descr>TRUE if the parameters have been successfully changed.</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="q_xWorking" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Change Operation in progress.</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="q_xFailed" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Change has failed.</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="q_xWrongInputs" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Inputs out of range</descr>
								</var>
							</outputVars>
