					<functionBlock name="EEVDAlarmMgmt" version="1.0.2" creationDate="1601478235" lastModifiedDate="1654769380" excludeFromBuild="FALSE" excludeFromBuildIfNotDef="">
						<title>Alarms from EEV driver management</title>
						<descr>&lt;HTML&gt;This AFB permits to exclude, filter and automatically rearm alarms in the EEV driver.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
For the TM172EVEV/EVEVD driver the meaning of bits for i_iAlarms is:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
Bit 0 - Chip does not respond - Detected error on bipolar driver chip: chip does not respond - Valve stops in current position &lt;br&gt;
Bit 1 -	Thermal shutdown - Detected error on bipolar driver chip: chip in fault protection - Moves the valve to the emergency position n30. Then any activity on the valve is stopped.&lt;br&gt;	
Bit 2 - Predriver detected error(*) - Detected error on bipolar driver chip: chip in fault protection - Moves the valve to the emergency position n30. Then any activity on thevalve is stopped.&lt;br&gt;					
Bit 3 -	Undervoltage Lockout(* )- Detected error on bipolar driver chip: chip in fault protection - Moves the valve to the emergency position n30. Then any activity on thevalve is stopped.&lt;br&gt;					
Bit 4 -	Reserved&lt;br&gt;
Bit 5 -	Overcurrent - Valve coil in short-circuit - Valve stops in current position – Alarm cause must be solved and a new “Activate and synchronize” command must be sent. &lt;br&gt;
Bit 6 -	Reserved&lt;br&gt;
Bit 7 -	Max number of valve direction changing (only if n12 &gt; 0) - Max number of valve direction changing achieved - Moves the valve to the emergency position n30. Then any activity on the valve is stopped.&lt;br&gt;
Bit 8 -	Quantity of TM172EVEVBAT/EVEVDBA connected &lt;&gt; parameter n36 value or TM172EVEVBAT/EVEVDBA exceeds charging time timeout	- TM172EVEVBAT/EVEVDBA inoperable - Non-blocking alarm&lt;br&gt;
Bit 9 -	Power supply outage if TM172EVEVBAT/EVEVDBA connected and charged with enough energy - Power supply not detected - Movement towards the emergency position n30 is executed only if n31=1 otherwise no action is done. If n17=0, the value of the  maximum speed in emergency closing  is equal to dE01. If n17 &gt;0 the movement towards the emergency position n30 is done using n17 speed&lt;br&gt;
Bit 10 - TM172EVEVBAT/EVEVDBA degraded due to the charge is too fast or if the last time that there has been an emergency movement followed by power fail, this has not been completed. The value has persisted in EEPROM so an emergency movement must be repeated successfully to cancel it. - TM172EVEVBAT/EVEVDBA degraded (*)&lt;br&gt;
Bit 11 - Configuration error n16 value not compatible with TM172EVEV/EVEVD model - Unipolar: n32, n33,n34, and n35 value combination not allowed - Bipolar: dE04&lt;0 and at least one of n27, n28, n29 not 0 - Configuration error	- Valve stops in current position – Alarm cause must be solved and a new activate command must be sent. Automatic rearm is managed by the AFB EEVDSettingsU or EEVDSettingsB after sending new parameter values.&lt;br&gt;
Bit 12 - Disconnection on W1+ or W1- - Valve disconnected - Driver moves the EEV in any case. The AFB EEVDCntrl by default considers this alarm as a stopping condition and try to move the valve to the ‘Alarm’ position, where the EEV rest until the alarm disappears. – The alarm is detected and/or reset only in synchronization phase. If detected, it will be active until the next synchronization, as the disconnection is checked again and alarm is confirmed or reset.&lt;br&gt;
Bit 13 - Disconnection on W2+ or W2- - Valve disconnected - Driver moves the EEV in any case. The AFB EEVDCntrl by default considers this alarm as a stopping condition and try to move the valve to the ‘Alarm’ position, where the EEV rest until the alarm disappears. – The alarm is detected and/or reset only in synchronization phase. If detected, it will be active until the next synchronization, as the disconnection is checked again and alarm is confirmed or reset.&lt;br&gt;				
Bit 14 - CAN not working, communication with master lost (not readable via CAN) - Loss of communication on CAN expansion bus. Detected only after first connection with CAN master controller	- Moves the valve to the emergency position n30. Then any activity on the valve is stopped.&lt;br&gt;
Bit 15 - Reserved&lt;br&gt;
(*) Contact your local support.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;
The meaning of bits of i_iStatus is supposed to be:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;
Bit 0 - Command received&lt;br&gt;
Bit 1 - Command completed&lt;br&gt;
Bit 2 - Command completed successfully&lt;br&gt;
Bit 3 - Action in progress can't be interrupted&lt;br&gt;
Bit 4 - Valve position is known&lt;br&gt;
Bit 8 - Error detected&lt;br&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;

For the variable pointed by i_ptriCommands the bit 0 is used to command an  activate and synchronize” action</descr>
						<vars>
							<inputVars>
								<var name="i_xEn" type="BOOL">
									<descr>T: block enabled F: block disabled, Out=FALSE</descr>
								</var>
								<var name="i_iAlarms" type="INT">
									<descr>Diagnostics from EEVD</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_wMaskExcludeAl" type="WORD">
									<descr>Bit mask to exclude alarms</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_iStatus" type="INT">
									<descr>Status from EEVD</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_wMaskFiltAl" type="WORD">
									<descr>Bit mask to filter alarms</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_udiTimeFilterAl" type="UDINT">
									<descr>Filter time for Alarms (ms Default: 10000)</descr>
									<initValue>10000</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_wMaskRearmAl" type="WORD">
									<descr>Bit mask to rearm alarms</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_udiTimeRearmAlarm" type="UDINT">
									<descr>Repeat time for rearm of alarms (ms Default: 30000)</descr>
									<initValue>30000</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="i_ptriCommands" type="@INT">
									<descr>pointer to Commands for EEVD</descr>
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
							</inputVars>
							<outputVars>
								<var name="q_xAlarm" type="BOOL">
									<descr>Alarm from EEVD</descr>
								</var>
							</outputVars>
							<externalVars>
								<var name="sysTimer" type="UDINT"/>
							</externalVars>
							<localVars>
								<var name="iAlarmFilt" type="INT"/>
								<var name="timeRearmAlarm" type="TON"/>
								<var name="xAlarmRearmOld" type="BOOL"/>
								<var name="usiSynchroCmdStatus" type="USINT"/>
								<var name="SETST_IDLE" type="USINT">
									<initValue>0</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="SETST_SEND" type="USINT">
									<initValue>1</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="SETST_SYNCRO" type="USINT">
									<initValue>2</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="SETST_WAIT_SYNCRO" type="USINT">
									<initValue>3</initValue>
								</var>
								<var name="usiAlarmSynchro" type="USINT"/>
								<var name="udiSavedTimer" type="UDINT"/>
								<var name="xResetAlarm" type="BOOL"/>
								<var name="iAlarmFiltOnly" type="INT"/>
								<var name="xOldFilter" type="BOOL"/>
								<var name="udiSavedTimerFilter" type="UDINT"/>
								<var name="xInit" type="BOOL">
									<initValue>TRUE</initValue>
								</var>
							</localVars>
						</vars>
