					<functionBlock name="EEVDSettingsB" version="1.1.4" creationDate="0" lastModifiedDate="1654700056" excludeFromBuild="FALSE" excludeFromBuildIfNotDef="">
						<title>EEV driver settings management for Bipolar valves</title>
						<descr>&lt;HTML&gt;This AFB is specific for the EEV driver for bipolar stepper valves and acts as an expansion for controller CPUs, exchanging data through CAN expansion bus.

The EEVDSettingsB AFB, instantiated as many times as there are bipolar valves is in charge of sending to the EEV driver associated to each valve the right settings selecting them from presets (internal or defined in a file), or using EEPROM parameters.
Settings will be pushed automatically at boot or set on PLC side during runtime.

Associated EEPROM PARAMETERS are overwritten with last set values if i_xSenfCfg = FALSE after a transition from a value &gt;0 to a value = 0 of dE00 parameter. 

The EEVDSettingsB AFB must be put inside the Background task of the PLC.</descr>
						<vars>
							<inputVars>
								<var name="i_xEn" type="BOOL">
									<descr>FB enable</descr>
									<initValue>FALSE</initValue>
								</var>
